  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_2 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [inst_4 : BorelSpace E] {V : E → ℝ} (κ : NNReal),\n  1 ≤ κ →\n    ContDiff ℝ 2 V →\n      (∀ (x w : E), (↑κ)⁻¹ * ‖w‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) w) w ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) w) w ≤ ‖w‖ ^ 2) →\n        0 < Module.finrank ℝ E →\n          ∀ (η : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E) → ℝ),\n            Measurable η →\n              ∀ (c Δ : ℝ),\n                0 < c →\n                  c < 1 / 4 →\n                    (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), 0 < η s ∧ η s ≤ c) →\n                      0 < Δ →\n                        Δ ≤ 1 / 2 →\n                          ∀ (s0 : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E))\n                            (M : ProbabilityTheory.Kernel (NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) E)\n                            [ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel M],\n                            have d := ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E);\n                            have K := fun r => (1 + r) / ((↑κ)⁻¹ + r);\n                            have τ := fun s => if 2 ≤ K ↑s.1 then K ↑s.1 else c;\n                            have L := 2 + Real.log (K ↑s0.1 * d * 2 / Δ);\n                            have B := 1 / 1024 / (√(d * L) + L);\n                            have J := ⌈8 * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * K ↑s0.1 / B)⌉₊;\n                            have _eps := Δ / √(↑J + 1);\n                            have v := fun s => (η s + τ s) / (1 + ↑s.1);\n                            have bp := fun s => s.1 + (v s)⁻¹.toNNReal;\n                            have obs := fun p => p.2.1 + √(τ p.1 / (1 + ↑p.1.1)) • p.2.2;\n                            have center := fun p => (↑(bp p.1))⁻¹ • (↑p.1.1 • p.1.2.1 + (v p.1)⁻¹ • obs p);\n                            have F := fun p x => V x + ↑(bp p.1) / 2 * ‖x - center p‖ ^ 2;\n                            have T := fun p x => x - (1 + ↑(bp p.1))⁻¹ • gradient (F p) x;\n                            have Qn := fun n p => ‖gradient (F p) ((T p)^[n] p.2.1)‖ ^ 2;\n                            have N := fun s =>\n                              if h : ∃ n, Qn n s ≤ (fun p => ((↑κ)⁻¹ + ↑(bp p.1)) * d) s then Nat.find h else 0;\n                            have update := fun p =>\n                              (bp p.1, center p, (T p)^[N p] p.2.1, p.1.2.2.2.1 + 1, fun n =>\n                                Nat.casesOn n (obs p) p.1.2.2.2.2);\n                            have bb := fun s => Max.max (↑s.1) B⁻¹;\n                            have TF := fun s x => V x + bb s / 2 * ‖x - s.2.1‖ ^ 2;\n                            have TT := fun s x => x - (1 + bb s)⁻¹ • gradient (TF s) x;\n                            have TQn := fun n s => ‖gradient (TF s) ((TT s)^[n] s.2.2.1)‖ ^ 2;\n                            have TN := fun s => if h : ∃ n, TQn n s ≤ (fun s => d * bb s) s then Nat.find h else 0;\n                            have txp := fun s => (TT s)^[TN s] s.2.2.1;\n                            have TA := fun s => (bb s)⁻¹;\n                            have tg := fun s => gradient V (txp s);\n                            have th := fun s => s.2.1 - TA s • tg s;\n                            have tnu :=\n                              (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Ioc 0 1)).prod\n                                (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                            have tW := fun s p =>\n                              Min.min 1\n                                (Max.max (-1)\n                                  (have s_1 := ((s, p.1), p.2).1.1;\n                                  have x := ((s, p.1), p.2).1.2;\n                                  have t := ((s, p.1), p.2).2.1;\n                                  have z := √(TA s_1) • ((s, p.1), p.2).2.2;\n                                  Inner.inner ℝ\n                                    ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                      (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * t) • (x - th s_1) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * t) • z))\n                                    (tg s_1 -\n                                      gradient V\n                                        (th s_1 + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * t) • (x - th s_1) +\n                                          Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * t) • z))));\n                            have tproposal := fun s =>\n                              MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => th s + √(TA s) • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                            have trho := fun s =>\n                              MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x =>\n                                (tproposal s).prod\n                                  ((ProbabilityTheory.poissonMeasure\n                                        ⟨2 * 1,\n                                          le_of_lt\n                                            (mul_pos\n                                              (Mathlib.Meta.Positivity.pos_of_isNat\n                                                (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ (Eq.refl 2))\n                                                (Eq.refl (Nat.ble 1 2)))\n                                              (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_lt_true\n                                                (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ Nat.cast_zero)\n                                                (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ Nat.cast_one)\n                                                (Eq.refl Bool.false)))⟩).prod\n                                    ((MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x => tnu).prod\n                                      (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Icc 0 1))));\n                            have _tpi := fun s =>\n                              (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => s.2.1 + √(TA s) • z)\n                                    (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).tilted\n                                fun x => -V x;\n                            have μV := MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.tilted fun x => -V x;\n                            MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μV ∧\n                              ∃ Lt P TG H,\n                                ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel Lt ∧\n                                  ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel P ∧\n                                    ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel TG ∧\n                                      ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel H ∧\n                                        (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                            P s =\n                                              if B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1 then MeasureTheory.Measure.dirac s\n                                              else\n                                                MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => update (s, z))\n                                                  ((M s).prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))) ∧\n                                          (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                              MeasureTheory.Measure.map\n                                                  (fun omega =>\n                                                    if h :\n                                                        ∃ n,\n                                                          omega n ∈\n                                                            {p |\n                                                              p.2.2.2 ≤\n                                                                ∏ i, (1 + tW s (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * 1)} then\n                                                      (omega (Nat.find h)).1\n                                                    else 0)\n                                                  (trho s) =\n                                                Lt s) ∧\n                                            (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                TG s = μV.tilted fun x => -(↑s.1 / 2) * ‖x - s.2.1‖ ^ 2) ∧\n                                              (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                  H s =\n                                                    MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun p => p.1 + p.2)\n                                                      ((TG s).prod\n                                                        (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √(v s) • z)\n                                                          (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)))) ∧\n                                                have Q := fun s =>\n                                                  MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun p => p.1 + p.2)\n                                                    ((M s).prod\n                                                      (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √(τ s / (1 + ↑s.1)) • z)\n                                                        (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)));\n                                                have e := fun s =>\n                                                  if B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1 then 0 else InformationTheory.klDiv (Q s) (H s);\n                                                Measurable e ∧\n                                                  ∀ (m : ℕ),\n                                                    InformationTheory.klDiv ((Lt.comp (P ^ (J + m))) s0) (TG s0) ≤\n                                                      ∑ j ∈ Finset.range J,\n                                                          ∫⁻ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), e s ∂(P ^ j) s0 +\n                                                        ENNReal.ofReal (Δ ^ 2 / (↑J + 1))",
    "statement_sha256": "40ecc48bc7c1419a3e1417c02a53c1822978e8415b4a3714fc5f478cc7d53129",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal is the type of nonnegative real numbers. Real.toNNReal truncates a real below at zero. Module.finrank is finite real vector-space dimension. fderiv is the Frechet derivative; gradient is the real inner-product gradient. Function.iterate applies its function the displayed natural number of times. Nat.find is the least natural satisfying the displayed existential predicate. Nat.casesOn defines a sequence by its zeroth value and shifted tail.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.Kernel is a jointly measurable transition interface; IsMarkovKernel says every input fiber is a probability measure. Kernel.comp R P first draws a state from P then an output from R. InformationTheory.klDiv is extended nonnegative relative entropy. Displayed nonnegative integrals take values in extended nonnegative reals,including infinity. No finiteness or absolute-continuity premise is implicit in the KL notation.",
      "Measure.map is pushforward and Measure.prod is independent product. stdGaussian is standard Gaussian on the displayed finite-dimensional inner-product space. MeasurableSet is with respect to the displayed Borel/measurable structure. The product type is right-associated; Nat-to-E is a full infinite sequence.",
      "Measure.tilted mu f denotes exponential reweighting by exp(f),normalized according to its Lean definition. The definition is total; probability and finite-normalization properties are not inferred from the notation alone. volume on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space denotes its canonical Lebesgue volume.",
      "Measure.infinitePi is the independent countable product of the displayed component probability measures. poissonMeasure lambda is the Poisson law with mean lambda. Restricted volume on a displayed real interval is the measure restriction,with the exact endpoints shown. Fin n indexes natural numbers from zero to n-1;its finite product is one when n=0. Nat.ceil is the natural ceiling operation. Kernel powers use composition and the identity kernel at exponent zero. All minimum,maximum,trigonometric,exponential and logarithm symbols retain their displayed real definitions; no source-specific convention is supplied."
    ]
